{"content":[{"c":["MOURNING"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Established ritual for grieving, observed by a dead person’s relatives and friends. It began with the closing of the eyes of the dead (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.4","r":"Gen.46.4","rawR":"Gen.46.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.4","value":"Gen.46.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:4"},"), the embracing of the body (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.50.1","r":"Gen.50.1","rawR":"Gen.50.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.50.1","value":"Gen.50.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"50:1"},"), and its preparation for burial. The hot climate necessitated that burial take place immediately (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.5.1-10","r":"Acts.5.1-10","rawR":"Acts.5.1-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.5.1-10","value":"Acts.5.1-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 5:1-10"},"). But detailed information about burial earlier than NT times (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.27.59","r":"Matt.27.59","rawR":"Matt.27.59","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.27.59","value":"Matt.27.59"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 27:59"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.11.44","r":"John.11.44","rawR":"John.11.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.44","value":"John.11.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 11:44"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.19.39-40","r":"John.19.39-40","rawR":"John.19.39-40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.19.39-40","value":"John.19.39-40"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:39-40"},") is extremely meager. Excavations suggest that the dead were buried fully clothed but not in coffins. The Israelites practiced neither embalming nor cremation, but decent burial was essential."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["At the news of a death, it was customary to tear one’s garments (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.37.34","r":"Gen.37.34","rawR":"Gen.37.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.37.34","value":"Gen.37.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 37:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.1.11","r":"2Sam.1.11","rawR":"2Sam.1.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.1.11","value":"2Sam.1.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 1:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.1.20","r":"Job.1.20","rawR":"Job.1.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.20","value":"Job.1.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 1:20"},"), put on sackcloth (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.3.31","r":"2Sam.3.31","rawR":"2Sam.3.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.3.31","value":"2Sam.3.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 3:31"},"), and take off one’s shoes (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.15.30","r":"2Sam.15.30","rawR":"2Sam.15.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.15.30","value":"2Sam.15.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 15:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mic.1.8","r":"Mic.1.8","rawR":"Mic.1.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.1.8","value":"Mic.1.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mi 1:8"},") and headdress; a man might cover his beard or veil his face (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.24.17,23","r":"Ezek.24.17,23","rawR":"Ezek.24.17,23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.24.17,23","value":"Ezek.24.17,23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 24:17, 23"},"). Mourners put earth on their heads (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.7.6","r":"Josh.7.6","rawR":"Josh.7.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.7.6","value":"Josh.7.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 7:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.4.12","r":"1Sam.4.12","rawR":"1Sam.4.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.4.12","value":"1Sam.4.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 4:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.9.1","r":"Neh.9.1","rawR":"Neh.9.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.9.1","value":"Neh.9.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 9:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.2.12","r":"Job.2.12","rawR":"Job.2.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.2.12","value":"Job.2.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 2:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.27.30","r":"Ezek.27.30","rawR":"Ezek.27.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.27.30","value":"Ezek.27.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 27:30"},") or rolled themselves in the dust (",{"href":"?bref=Job.16.15","r":"Job.16.15","rawR":"Job.16.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.16.15","value":"Job.16.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 16:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mic.1.10","r":"Mic.1.10","rawR":"Mic.1.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.1.10","value":"Mic.1.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mi 1:10"},") or sat on a heap of ashes (",{"href":"?bref=Esth.4.3","r":"Esth.4.3","rawR":"Esth.4.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Esth.4.3","value":"Esth.4.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Est 4:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.58.5","r":"Isa.58.5","rawR":"Isa.58.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.58.5","value":"Isa.58.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 58:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.6.26","r":"Jer.6.26","rawR":"Jer.6.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.6.26","value":"Jer.6.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 6:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.27.30","r":"Ezek.27.30","rawR":"Ezek.27.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.27.30","value":"Ezek.27.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 27:30"},"). Such mourning rites as shaving the hair and the beard and making cuts on the body (",{"href":"?bref=Job.1.20","r":"Job.1.20","rawR":"Job.1.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.20","value":"Job.1.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 1:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.22.12","r":"Isa.22.12","rawR":"Isa.22.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.22.12","value":"Isa.22.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 22:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.16.6","r":"Jer.16.6","rawR":"Jer.16.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.16.6","value":"Jer.16.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 16:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.41.5","r":"Jer.41.5","rawR":"Jer.41.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.41.5","value":"Jer.41.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"41:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.47.5","r":"Jer.47.5","rawR":"Jer.47.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.47.5","value":"Jer.47.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"47:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.48.37","r":"Jer.48.37","rawR":"Jer.48.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.48.37","value":"Jer.48.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"48:37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.7.18","r":"Ezek.7.18","rawR":"Ezek.7.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.7.18","value":"Ezek.7.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 7:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.8.10","r":"Amos.8.10","rawR":"Amos.8.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.8.10","value":"Amos.8.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 8:10"},") were condemned (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.19.27-28","r":"Lev.19.27-28","rawR":"Lev.19.27-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.19.27-28","value":"Lev.19.27-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 19:27-28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.14.1","r":"Deut.14.1","rawR":"Deut.14.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.14.1","value":"Deut.14.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 14:1"},") because of pagan associations. Mourners refrained from washing and discontinued the use of perfumes (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.12.20","r":"2Sam.12.20","rawR":"2Sam.12.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.12.20","value":"2Sam.12.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 12:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.14.2","r":"2Sam.14.2","rawR":"2Sam.14.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.14.2","value":"2Sam.14.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Fasting was also a mourning rite (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.31.13","r":"1Sam.31.13","rawR":"1Sam.31.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.31.13","value":"1Sam.31.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 31:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.1.12","r":"2Sam.1.12","rawR":"2Sam.1.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.1.12","value":"2Sam.1.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 1:12"},"). Neighbors or friends brought mourning bread and the “cup of consolation” to the relatives of the deceased (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.16.7","r":"Jer.16.7","rawR":"Jer.16.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.16.7","value":"Jer.16.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 16:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.24.17,22","r":"Ezek.24.17,22","rawR":"Ezek.24.17,22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.24.17,22","value":"Ezek.24.17,22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 24:17, 22"},"). Food could not be prepared at the house of the dead because death rendered a place unclean. The dead were unclean to the extent that a priest could “profane” himself by taking part in mourning rites, except for his nearest blood relatives (mother, father, son, daughter, brother, and sister, provided she was still a virgin; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.21.1-4,10-11","r":"Lev.21.1-4,10-11","rawR":"Lev.21.1-4,10-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.21.1-4,10-11","value":"Lev.21.1-4,10-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 21:1-4, 10-11"},"). These mourning rites were not acts of worship directed toward the dead, nor did they constitute a cult for the dead, but rather they were expressions of grief and affection."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["At the graveside, lamentation for the dead was made (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.13.30","r":"1Kgs.13.30","rawR":"1Kgs.13.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.13.30","value":"1Kgs.13.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 13:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.6.26","r":"Jer.6.26","rawR":"Jer.6.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.6.26","value":"Jer.6.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 6:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.5.16","r":"Amos.5.16","rawR":"Amos.5.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.5.16","value":"Amos.5.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 5:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.8.10","r":"Amos.8.10","rawR":"Amos.8.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.8.10","value":"Amos.8.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Zech.12.10","r":"Zech.12.10","rawR":"Zech.12.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.12.10","value":"Zech.12.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zec 12:10"},") by men and women in separate groups (",{"href":"?bref=Zech.12.11-14","r":"Zech.12.11-14","rawR":"Zech.12.11-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.12.11-14","value":"Zech.12.11-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zec 12:11-14"},"). These exclamations of sorrow might develop into a rhythmic lament (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.1.17-27","r":"2Sam.1.17-27","rawR":"2Sam.1.17-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.1.17-27","value":"2Sam.1.17-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 1:17-27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.8.10","r":"Amos.8.10","rawR":"Amos.8.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.8.10","value":"Amos.8.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 8:10"},"). However, professional mourners, men and especially women (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.9.17-19","r":"Jer.9.17-19","rawR":"Jer.9.17-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.9.17-19","value":"Jer.9.17-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 9:17-19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.5.16","r":"Amos.5.16","rawR":"Amos.5.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.5.16","value":"Amos.5.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 5:16"},"), were employed. The book of Lamentations is a fine example of laments and is a reminder that among Jews mourning was not always associated with death. It expressed brokenness of spirit for sin, individual and national. National calamity also evoked great lamentation."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["These mourning rites were expressive of great grief. But some of them—tearing clothes, wearing sackcloth, disfiguring oneself with dust and ashes, self-mutilation—point to paroxysms of grief, the religious significance of which now escapes us. This was far removed from mourning as an inner feeling or a mood of the mind. It was not just an involuntary outburst of feeling but rather a deliberate, established ritual. When death occurred, the Israelite wept because it was customary and seemly. The erection of monuments or memorials was not unknown (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.18.18","r":"2Sam.18.18","rawR":"2Sam.18.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.18.18","value":"2Sam.18.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 18:18"},"), but the average Israelite was too poor for this to be a common practice."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Mourning practices in NT times differed little from those described in the OT. Mourning was associated with Christ’s second advent (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.24.30","r":"Matt.24.30","rawR":"Matt.24.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.24.30","value":"Matt.24.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 24:30"},"), with repentance (",{"href":"?bref=Jas.4.8-10","r":"Jas.4.8-10","rawR":"Jas.4.8-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jas.4.8-10","value":"Jas.4.8-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jas 4:8-10"},"), with Christ’s leaving the 12 (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.9.15","r":"Matt.9.15","rawR":"Matt.9.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.9.15","value":"Matt.9.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 9:15"},"), with deep spirituality (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.5.4","r":"Matt.5.4","rawR":"Matt.5.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.5.4","value":"Matt.5.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:4"},"), as well as with death (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.5.38-39","r":"Mark.5.38-39","rawR":"Mark.5.38-39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.5.38-39","value":"Mark.5.38-39"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 5:38-39"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.7.13","r":"Luke.7.13","rawR":"Luke.7.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.7.13","value":"Luke.7.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 7:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.11.33","r":"John.11.33","rawR":"John.11.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.11.33","value":"John.11.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 11:33"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["True, the overthrow of death by Jesus Christ robbed death of its sting and the grave of its victory (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.15.54-57","r":"1Cor.15.54-57","rawR":"1Cor.15.54-57","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.15.54-57","value":"1Cor.15.54-57"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 15:54-57"},"), but the Christian still mourns, though not as those who have no hope (",{"href":"?bref=1Thes.4.13","r":"1Thes.4.13","rawR":"1Thes.4.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Thes.4.13","value":"1Thes.4.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 4:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.21.4","r":"Rev.21.4","rawR":"Rev.21.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.21.4","value":"Rev.21.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rv 21:4"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=BurialBurialCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"BurialBurialCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"BurialBurialCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Burial, Burial Customs"},"; ",{"href":"?item=FuneralCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"FuneralCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"FuneralCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Funeral Customs"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Mourning","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 46:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.4","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.4","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.4"},{"anchorText":"50:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.50.1","rawQueryValue":"Gen.50.1","sourceRefExact":"Gen.50.1"},{"anchorText":"Acts 5:1-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.5.1-10","rawQueryValue":"Acts.5.1-10","sourceRefExact":"Acts.5.1-10"},{"anchorText":"Mt 27:59","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.27.59","rawQueryValue":"Matt.27.59","sourceRefExact":"Matt.27.59"},{"anchorText":"Jn 11:44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.11.44","rawQueryValue":"John.11.44","sourceRefExact":"John.11.44"},{"anchorText":"19:39-40","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.19.39-40","rawQueryValue":"John.19.39-40","sourceRefExact":"John.19.39-40"},{"anchorText":"Gn 37:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.37.34","rawQueryValue":"Gen.37.34","sourceRefExact":"Gen.37.34"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 1:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.1.11","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.1.11","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.1.11"},{"anchorText":"Jb 1:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.1.20","rawQueryValue":"Job.1.20","sourceRefExact":"Job.1.20"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 3:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.3.31","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.3.31","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.3.31"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 15:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.15.30","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.15.30","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.15.30"},{"anchorText":"Mi 1:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mic.1.8","rawQueryValue":"Mic.1.8","sourceRefExact":"Mic.1.8"},{"anchorText":"Ez 24:17, 23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.24.17,23","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.24.17,23","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.24.17,23"},{"anchorText":"Jos 7:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.7.6","rawQueryValue":"Josh.7.6","sourceRefExact":"Josh.7.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 4:12",